1
00:00:16,727 --> 00:00:24,713
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in terms of not-self, a person can get the idea that...

2
00:00:24,814 --> 00:00:25,694
[SPEAKER_00]: Most people have...

3
00:00:25,754 --> 00:00:29,437
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, a normal human being knows they are going to die.

4
00:00:30,618 --> 00:00:38,525
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they know, without reflecting that much, I'm not in control of my body fully, you know.

5
00:00:40,526 --> 00:00:44,409
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they get that idea that it's not mine.

6
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:46,351
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, I'm not in control.

7
00:00:49,136 --> 00:00:52,939
[SPEAKER_00]: But they don't... they don't understand not-self.

8
00:00:53,279 --> 00:00:54,560
[SPEAKER_00]: They still take things personally.

9
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:56,221
[SPEAKER_00]: They still take the body personally.

10
00:00:56,441 --> 00:00:56,641
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

11
00:00:56,921 --> 00:00:59,783
[SPEAKER_00]: Even though you know, overall, you're going to die.

12
00:00:59,803 --> 00:00:59,963
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

13
00:01:01,044 --> 00:01:01,704
[SPEAKER_01]: So, why is that?

14
00:01:05,947 --> 00:01:08,769
[SPEAKER_00]: I was supposed to say, they haven't really thought about it deep enough.

15
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:11,411
[SPEAKER_00]: Or contemplated.

16
00:01:11,691 --> 00:01:12,111
[SPEAKER_01]: Mm-hmm.

17
00:01:12,491 --> 00:01:13,452
[SPEAKER_00]: But... And...

18
00:01:13,512 --> 00:01:14,172
[SPEAKER_00]: Some people did.

19
00:01:14,933 --> 00:01:16,494
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's still being infatuated with life.

20
00:01:17,457 --> 00:01:18,938
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of how they act.

21
00:01:19,459 --> 00:01:20,279
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly, yeah.

22
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:23,362
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they act as though it is theirs.

23
00:01:23,582 --> 00:01:32,530
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you can have all the ideas you want, but if your behavior is not mirroring those ideas, that's where you're fueling those wrong assumptions.

24
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:39,776
[SPEAKER_01]: So, on one end, yes, when you're, you know, thinking clearly, you recognize all these characteristics of existence,

25
00:01:40,545 --> 00:01:57,135
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, out of habits and carelessness, the body still goes towards sensuality, resists discomfort, indulges in food, doesn't practice sense restraint, and that's the cesspit of the... that's the like the... the roots where your wrong views are being fed from.

26
00:01:58,136 --> 00:02:08,222
[SPEAKER_01]: So, although your ideas are, you know, different to that, you're actually going about things, it's very much accordance to sense of control and I'm gonna live forever.

27
00:02:09,488 --> 00:02:12,992
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, you need to have the right ideas, but now you need to start doing them.

28
00:02:14,193 --> 00:02:19,939
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to start doing the right... You need to start... like, you need to purify your behavior, as the Buddha said, to mirror those ideas.

29
00:02:21,581 --> 00:02:29,529
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, yeah, and it's like... exactly, that's... and that's why there were summoners and brahmins outside of the Buddha's teaching, who did actually...

30
00:02:30,222 --> 00:02:31,403
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your sense of control.

31
00:02:31,563 --> 00:02:32,744
[SPEAKER_01]: It can end at any moment.

32
00:02:32,764 --> 00:02:34,206
[SPEAKER_01]: And he said that's like the foremost of the outsider's views.

33
00:02:47,049 --> 00:03:02,906
[SPEAKER_01]: And the point was that, now, if you actually, not just think that view once a month, or be convinced that you're holder of that view, but, okay, start, whenever you want to act towards the world, towards him, her, or this or that, you first put that view.

34
00:03:03,988 --> 00:03:06,809
[SPEAKER_01]: That you're nothing to no one anywhere in the world and nobody's nothing.

35
00:03:06,969 --> 00:03:11,650
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's just, oh, you would not be able to engage in passion, aversion, distraction.

36
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:20,251
[SPEAKER_01]: And there were then people who made the effort and their behavior did start to correspond to those views.

37
00:03:20,892 --> 00:03:27,673
[SPEAKER_01]: And those were the people that Buddha met in the suttas who needed very little instruction for final liberation, because they did a great amount of work already.

38
00:03:32,021 --> 00:03:34,202
[SPEAKER_00]: So, for example, if...

39
00:03:34,242 --> 00:03:42,145
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I might logically or reason that feelings are not mine because they're always changing and, you know, what do I feel now?

40
00:03:42,185 --> 00:03:43,685
[SPEAKER_00]: I feel pain now, I feel pleasure.

41
00:03:44,746 --> 00:03:46,126
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah, yeah, I can see that now.

42
00:03:46,566 --> 00:03:47,147
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, I can...

43
00:03:48,387 --> 00:03:50,190
[SPEAKER_00]: I can even record all my feelings.

44
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:50,510
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

45
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:51,752
[SPEAKER_00]: Ten o'clock was like this.

46
00:03:52,032 --> 00:03:52,573
[SPEAKER_00]: What's the time now?

47
00:03:52,593 --> 00:03:54,055
[SPEAKER_01]: Collect information about it.

48
00:03:54,095 --> 00:03:54,515
[SPEAKER_01]: Study it.

49
00:03:54,555 --> 00:03:55,376
[SPEAKER_01]: And I can see.

50
00:03:55,677 --> 00:03:56,338
[SPEAKER_00]: Definitely, yes.

51
00:03:56,698 --> 00:03:59,281
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's it's kind of mirrors at right view.

52
00:04:00,203 --> 00:04:01,184
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, on paper.

53
00:04:01,264 --> 00:04:02,165
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

54
00:04:02,225 --> 00:04:02,746
[SPEAKER_00]: In theory.

55
00:04:03,667 --> 00:04:06,611
[SPEAKER_01]: But... Well, that's in the nutshell, Abhidhamma and commentaries, basically.

56
00:04:07,799 --> 00:04:13,084
[SPEAKER_01]: It's that impersonal take, almost like a scientific collection of observational facts of the Buddhist teachings.

57
00:04:13,184 --> 00:04:15,826
[SPEAKER_01]: It's all this, like, the list and comparisons and permutations.

58
00:04:16,707 --> 00:04:19,349
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not the dhamma, because... Go on.

59
00:04:19,489 --> 00:04:20,670
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I see that it's...

60
00:04:20,851 --> 00:04:27,857
[SPEAKER_00]: I understand in theory that it's impermanent, or inaccessible to my control, the feeling.

61
00:04:28,537 --> 00:04:32,961
[SPEAKER_00]: But now, as I feel, what do I do when I'm feeling pain?

62
00:04:33,382 --> 00:04:33,562
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

63
00:04:34,630 --> 00:04:35,311
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, I must...

64
00:04:35,671 --> 00:04:37,392
[SPEAKER_00]: I must... Am I trying to get rid of it?

65
00:04:38,032 --> 00:04:39,213
[SPEAKER_00]: Or am I unmoved by it?

66
00:04:39,694 --> 00:04:45,358
[SPEAKER_01]: I must graft that idea onto... Inevitably, you'll be trying to get rid of it through using those ideas, yeah.

67
00:04:47,419 --> 00:04:54,745
[SPEAKER_01]: But, if you then really start to understand those ideas, you realize, yeah, thinking about the dhamma does not mean that's the dhamma.

68
00:04:55,705 --> 00:05:00,349
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can have all the ideas, but if you're not actually applying it rightly, there is no dhamma there.

69
00:05:01,093 --> 00:05:09,497
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's important to recognize because otherwise people can easily slip into a view of, well, as long as I think about the dhamma, I am on the path.

70
00:05:10,458 --> 00:05:10,898
[SPEAKER_01]: But you're not.

71
00:05:11,158 --> 00:05:12,779
[SPEAKER_01]: You're on the path when you become a sotāpanna.

72
00:05:13,019 --> 00:05:14,260
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the beginning of the path.

73
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:17,381
[SPEAKER_01]: Not if you don't see the dhamma means you don't see the path.

74
00:05:17,441 --> 00:05:19,202
[SPEAKER_01]: How can you be on the path if you don't see the path?

75
00:05:21,063 --> 00:05:24,005
[SPEAKER_01]: And you will not become a sotāpanna just on account of such ideas.

76
00:05:24,265 --> 00:05:28,707
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to actually start applying them and enduing things on the right level.

77
00:05:29,727 --> 00:05:34,909
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I say, well, feelings are not mine, not my personal things.

78
00:05:34,929 --> 00:05:35,109
[SPEAKER_00]: Great.

79
00:05:35,129 --> 00:05:35,490
[SPEAKER_00]: Theory.

80
00:05:36,130 --> 00:05:37,050
[SPEAKER_01]: You got it.

81
00:05:37,230 --> 00:05:37,831
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what do you do?

82
00:05:37,871 --> 00:05:42,233
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, I'm feeling a lot of pain or prospect of pleasure, a lot of pleasure.

83
00:05:42,993 --> 00:05:44,774
[SPEAKER_00]: So, let's say there is a prospect of pleasure.

84
00:05:44,954 --> 00:05:46,594
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, let me apply that.

85
00:05:47,375 --> 00:05:50,056
[SPEAKER_01]: And what do you do in the face of prospect of pleasure?

86
00:05:52,497 --> 00:05:53,397
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't delight in it.

87
00:05:55,238 --> 00:05:56,779
[SPEAKER_01]: And, what else?

88
00:05:57,819 --> 00:05:59,240
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you act towards it?

89
00:06:00,483 --> 00:06:00,623
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

90
00:06:01,064 --> 00:06:01,444
[SPEAKER_01]: Follow it.

91
00:06:01,764 --> 00:06:02,385
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, so you endure it.

92
00:06:02,665 --> 00:06:03,125
[SPEAKER_01]: For how long?

93
00:06:05,347 --> 00:06:05,688
[SPEAKER_00]: Forever.

94
00:06:06,388 --> 00:06:06,729
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

95
00:06:07,549 --> 00:06:07,910
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

96
00:06:08,390 --> 00:06:14,696
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if those are the truths that you understood, that you accepted, that you intellectually verified as correct, now you start doing it.

97
00:06:15,196 --> 00:06:16,277
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this thing is not mine?

98
00:06:17,565 --> 00:06:18,005
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but it's...

99
00:06:18,345 --> 00:06:19,286
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not in my control.

100
00:06:19,586 --> 00:06:20,166
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a trap.

101
00:06:20,527 --> 00:06:21,127
[SPEAKER_01]: It's suffering.

102
00:06:21,267 --> 00:06:21,527
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

103
00:06:22,067 --> 00:06:22,327
[SPEAKER_01]: Great.

104
00:06:23,128 --> 00:06:23,528
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, do it.

105
00:06:23,608 --> 00:06:28,451
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's saying... but... but I'm... say... say, in the beginning, I am faced with feeling it.

106
00:06:28,831 --> 00:06:30,031
[SPEAKER_00]: This feeling is pressuring me.

107
00:06:30,051 --> 00:06:31,152
[SPEAKER_00]: It's touching me.

108
00:06:31,452 --> 00:06:33,073
[SPEAKER_00]: It does feel like mine.

109
00:06:33,173 --> 00:06:34,714
[SPEAKER_00]: But I have the outside view of the Buddha.

110
00:06:34,734 --> 00:06:35,494
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have an op...

111
00:06:35,614 --> 00:06:35,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

112
00:06:35,974 --> 00:06:36,915
[SPEAKER_01]: But you have an option now.

113
00:06:37,155 --> 00:06:38,716
[SPEAKER_01]: It feels like yours.

114
00:06:38,936 --> 00:06:40,817
[SPEAKER_01]: And the option there is, okay, so what do you do?

115
00:06:41,057 --> 00:06:42,658
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you accept the pressure that it's yours?

116
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:44,718
[SPEAKER_01]: Or do you not accept it?

117
00:06:44,799 --> 00:06:45,199
[SPEAKER_01]: It's mine.

118
00:06:45,599 --> 00:06:46,539
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah, look, this is yours.

119
00:06:46,679 --> 00:06:53,563
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you know, when when the fisherman throws a bait with the food, it's for the fish.

120
00:06:53,923 --> 00:06:54,363
[SPEAKER_01]: It's yours.

121
00:06:54,603 --> 00:06:55,604
[SPEAKER_01]: Take it.

122
00:06:55,844 --> 00:06:58,725
[SPEAKER_01]: So that you get hooked.

123
00:06:58,745 --> 00:07:00,906
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I accept the pressure, the bait.

124
00:07:01,066 --> 00:07:01,446
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

125
00:07:01,466 --> 00:07:03,607
[SPEAKER_00]: You accept the pressure, you accept the bait.

126
00:07:03,627 --> 00:07:05,788
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, sorry, I accept that there is pressure.

127
00:07:06,469 --> 00:07:07,969
[SPEAKER_00]: There is, that is a bait.

128
00:07:08,450 --> 00:07:09,030
[SPEAKER_00]: But I don't.

129
00:07:09,722 --> 00:07:14,746
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you might not necessarily see the bait, but you can already understand it by not acting out of pressure.

130
00:07:15,646 --> 00:07:17,067
[SPEAKER_01]: You are safe in regard to the bait.

131
00:07:18,488 --> 00:07:24,893
[SPEAKER_01]: You might not see it immediately, but at least you know, as long as I don't take this, there will be no bait I'm hooked with.

132
00:07:27,915 --> 00:07:36,321
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why I say it's important to recognize that dhamma begins with sotāpatti, not with the ideas of dhamma and even the clarity you might have.

133
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:48,145
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you do, you will be creating that discrepancy between your ideas that you're convinced are putting you on the path of dhamma, and your behavior that it's still not matching it.

134
00:07:48,886 --> 00:08:00,752
[SPEAKER_01]: Your lack of endurance, your lack of recognition at the right level, lack of restraint in regard to need to manage discomfort and unpleasant things.

135
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:17,102
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you don't have such view, and you recognize, yeah, these ideas, as clear and as pleasing as they are, they might be very right, and I might verify later on that I was spot-on right from the start, but the only way I'll do that...

136
00:08:18,467 --> 00:08:23,431
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not about, you know, through holding these views about the ideas and so on, and feeling saved on account of it.

137
00:08:23,972 --> 00:08:24,572
[SPEAKER_01]: No, it's okay.

138
00:08:24,672 --> 00:08:28,035
[SPEAKER_01]: Now let me do that in regard to sensuality, aversion and distraction.

139
00:08:28,175 --> 00:08:29,577
[SPEAKER_01]: Only three things.

140
00:08:29,597 --> 00:08:31,879
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't need to seek the verification anywhere else.

141
00:08:32,119 --> 00:08:33,920
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's how you... yeah, well, that's how you verify.

142
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,502
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

143
00:08:35,962 --> 00:08:39,505
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how you can only... you will ever only be able to verify.

144
00:08:39,765 --> 00:08:42,968
[SPEAKER_00]: So when things pressure you... Because I can have a view and you can agree with my view.

145
00:08:43,369 --> 00:08:43,549
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

146
00:08:44,069 --> 00:08:45,850
[SPEAKER_00]: We can both agree that feelings are not self.

147
00:08:45,870 --> 00:08:54,854
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, and we can write scholarly papers on it, and dissertations, and pages and pages of references, and create a whole network of information.

148
00:08:55,734 --> 00:08:56,495
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not the dhamma.

149
00:08:56,635 --> 00:08:57,976
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the information of the dhamma.

150
00:08:58,956 --> 00:09:00,917
[SPEAKER_01]: Dhamma is when things are endured on the right level.

151
00:09:03,198 --> 00:09:06,760
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I understand feelings are not myself.

152
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:08,640
[SPEAKER_00]: They don't belong to me.

153
00:09:09,381 --> 00:09:10,942
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, they just come and go.

154
00:09:11,562 --> 00:09:11,842
[SPEAKER_01]: Great.

155
00:09:13,490 --> 00:09:19,473
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, when things come and go, let them come and go without acting out of them, without trying to get rid of them, without delighting them, without welcoming them.

156
00:09:23,255 --> 00:09:24,035
[SPEAKER_00]: And keep doing it.

157
00:09:24,135 --> 00:09:24,816
[SPEAKER_01]: For as long as it takes.

158
00:09:25,936 --> 00:09:26,797
[SPEAKER_01]: And it might take forever.

159
00:09:28,338 --> 00:09:29,518
[SPEAKER_00]: And, eh... yeah.

160
00:09:29,778 --> 00:09:40,704
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in a way, the verification that has worked is the fact that feelings no longer pressure you.

161
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:43,641
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, eventually, yes, exactly.

162
00:09:43,841 --> 00:09:44,301
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, of course.

163
00:09:45,362 --> 00:09:50,605
[SPEAKER_01]: Just even the pressure felt will not be... well, it will diminish.

164
00:09:50,905 --> 00:09:52,186
[SPEAKER_01]: There will be no pressure in the end.

165
00:09:53,767 --> 00:10:03,313
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why, like, contact cannot... pāsa, the pressure, contact, whatever you translate it, cannot pressure the groundless one, when there is no ground to apply that pressure for an arahant.

166
00:10:05,714 --> 00:10:11,438
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he... arahant is unable,

167
00:10:12,883 --> 00:10:20,630
[SPEAKER_01]: To experience pressure of any kind anymore, mentally.

168
00:10:20,670 --> 00:10:22,511
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he's beyond.

169
00:10:22,532 --> 00:10:23,332
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing can pressure him.

170
00:10:25,594 --> 00:10:27,596
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there's nothing for him anymore.

171
00:10:29,998 --> 00:10:31,039
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, yeah.

172
00:10:31,159 --> 00:10:38,926
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that determination of self, that thing that determines self, is no longer there.

173
00:10:39,768 --> 00:10:41,909
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but now we're getting a bit abstract.

174
00:10:42,289 --> 00:10:47,810
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you know, you can speculate about it, but... No, because he endured things sufficiently on the right level.

175
00:10:48,630 --> 00:10:51,671
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why nothing can pressure him anymore.

176
00:10:51,751 --> 00:10:53,812
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's the difference, as I said many times before.

177
00:10:54,272 --> 00:10:59,353
[SPEAKER_01]: When pressure arises, people use even the dhamma to get rid of the pressure.

178
00:10:59,874 --> 00:11:02,454
[SPEAKER_01]: Not to endure it and understand it through enduring.

179
00:11:03,435 --> 00:11:04,575
[SPEAKER_01]: No, to get rid of it.

180
00:11:05,315 --> 00:11:08,236
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why they're not enduring it rightly, and that's why that's not the dhamma.

181
00:11:09,448 --> 00:11:11,579
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why that's management versus uprooting.

